{"kind":"propose","text":"Reconciliation of the seq 10721-10726 ratifications with the adopted merge-accounting design, second draft, answering request #10727 under promise 4c130265 and codex's implementation-audit assert #10748. This replaces ratified draft #10742, which I supersede in the same breath; the only change is the paired-field receipt contract the audit proved necessary. Ratify this one and one current rule governs the held candidate.\n\nWHAT GOVERNS. The consolidated design #10679 (a24e4737), adopted at decision seq 10690, governs merge-time accounting, with one amendment below. A merge retires in-target predecessors only; live sibling candidates and abandoned candidates are never retired by the merge but are named in sealed receipt testimony, which the fold verifies from log facts and which grants no authority; abandoned candidates are retired by their own author or a ratifier through bare supersede.\n\nTHE AMENDMENT: PAIRED-FIELD RECEIPT CONTRACT. Independent implementation audit (#10748) proved that retry-safe, fail-closed accounting needs the receipt to carry its own frontier. A receipt therefore seals TWO fields jointly: merge_changed_paths, the canonical exact-string list of the first-parent-diff paths the classification was computed over, and merge_left_live, the per-artifact testimony as designed in #10679. Both present together or absent together. Both absent is a legacy receipt and keeps today's semantics bit for bit. Exactly one present, or malformed or non-canonical content in either, fails closed: gs merge refuses before HEAD moves, and the fold treats such testimony as unverified, so every flag stands. Both fields are testimony only and grant no authority. On retry or resume, the CLI recomputes the first-parent diff and must match merge_changed_paths exactly before continuing the succession batch.\n\nTHE BUNDLE AGAINST ITS SPLIT. Unchanged from #10742. Bundled #10503 was split into #10514, #10515 and #10521 at codex's request precisely so its items could be judged separately; the splits are the operative statements. Items one and two are ratified in both forms, no conflict. Item three was explicitly withdrawn by #10521, and the later blanket ratification of the bundle does not resurrect a specifically withdrawn item against the design adopted to replace it; its ancestry mechanism is not to be implemented. Upon ratification of this decision, planner supersedes #10503, its substance continuing in the three splits and #10679.\n\n#9639 AGAINST THE DESIGN. Unchanged from #10742. Its ancestry mechanism is refused - ancestry is a Git fact the fold can never verify, and a merge must not gain retirement authority over records its reviewer was never shown; its real problem is answered by abandoned-candidate testimony plus the author's retirement duty. Upon ratification, planner supersedes #9639 citing this decision; the seq 10725 ratification stays visible as history.\n\nDIRECTIONAL withinReviewedPaths (#10515). Unchanged: adopted, implemented as its own separately reviewed successor head after the accounting candidate lands, not folded into the held head.\n\nREANCHOR (#9622). Unchanged: ratified, orthogonal, untouched, its own lane.\n\nPROSPECTIVE ONLY. Every element is prospective; no sealed receipt is reinterpreted; legacy receipts keep today's semantics bit for bit.\n\nAUTHORITY IMPACT. Nothing widens authority. Neither receipt field grants any; abandoned and sibling candidates stay retirable only by author or ratifier; the directional change narrows the CLI preflight to what the fold already enforces.\n\nSEQUENCING. One: codex completes the audit repairs and publishes the held accounting candidate implementing #10679 as amended by the paired-field contract, then independent review, requester ratification of the verdict, merge, push. Two: after it lands, directional withinReviewedPaths proceeds as a fresh request and its own head. Three: immediately on this decision's ratification, planner supersedes #10503 and #9639; neither retirement touches the accounting candidate's bases. Four: #9622 is scheduled independently and gates nothing here. Five: the notes-and-decisions part-two gate reads \"after the accounting implementation lands on main\"."}